WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070
There's so many new beauty releases

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.220
happening all the time,

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.350
so we gathered some of
the most hyped products

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.363
from December to test for ourselves.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.040
We're starting off with
these Infinite Chrome Flakes

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.340
from Danessa Myricks.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.020
This product is so interesting.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.850
I thought it would be more like a gel,

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.870
but it's actually this super
liquidy and flaky formula,

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.450
which made me really nervous.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.880
I used a brush to apply it

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.945
and the way the color shifts
with these flakes is unreal.

00:00:26.945 --> 00:00:28.150
It was kind of hard to get it to show

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.420
all of the colors on camera,

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.840
but you can see it here
on this hand swatch I did.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.000
It's so cool.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.650
It is supposed to have that texture,

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.200
so if you hate that, don't get this,

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.820
but I like the effect, and
I actually got no fallout.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.890
Like, once it dried, it did not move.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.620
It does have a slight tightening
feeling as it's drying,

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.740
but once it was fully dry,

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.780
it was totally comfortable on the eyes.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.920
I have a Patrick Ta blush
that I already love,

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.680
so I knew I would love this blush palette.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.870
It comes with three shades

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.000
in both cream and powder formulas.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.010
This Barbie pink color was speaking to me,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.210
so I went for that one.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.400
The pigment in these
blushes is incredible.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.080
Like, you can really build
these up, no problem.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.560
The cream blush blends really
well on top of foundation,

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.180
but I did get some patchiness

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.300
when I went over it with the powder one.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.700
I think you just need to be careful

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.490
with how much pressure you're using.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.860
I'm super heavy-handed
when it comes to my makeup.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.560
And make sure you're tapping
the blush in and not swiping.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.300
I think I prefer to wear the
cream and powder separately

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.830
rather than layered, but I
love the formulas of both.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.730
This is the Moira Diamond
Daze Liquid Shadow.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:25.910
I thought I was going to love these,

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:27.900
because I've seen so
many people try them out,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.120
and they look amazing,
really great price point,

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.060
but I could not get this
liquid shadow to behave.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.120
At first, I thought I could apply it

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.600
and then blend it out with my finger,

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.430
but that was just
removing all the product.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.350
So then I just applied
it with the applicator

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.770
like the instructions said,

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:45.720
but I had all these harsh edges
I just could not blend out.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.140
It's giving Monster High.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.000
It's giving ghouls and goblins.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.580
But nevertheless, she persisted,

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.150
and I tried it out a third time,

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:54.270
and it looked better, but not great.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.930
I'm not a liquid shadow kind of person,

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.150
so it could just be me,

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.620
but I've never tried a liquid shadow

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.390
that's this difficult to use.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.890
Please tell me what I'm doing wrong.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.440
You guys keep selling this out,

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.400
but I finally, finally got my hands

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.920
on the Charlotte Tilbury
Glowgasm Beauty Light Wand

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.630
in Pinkgasm,

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:14.380
which is the blushy pink shade
everyone is obsessed with.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.900
I'm going to say this:
The girls weren't lying.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.400
It's so, so good.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.920
Blending it was so effortless.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:24.460
It gives your cheeks this
glowy, flush look. Oh, my God.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.130
And none of the foundation
underneath moved or got patchy,

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.620
and I had already powdered
my face at this point.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.780
The second this comes
back in stock, get it.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.160
Next up is a product I
actually already use,

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.210
the Milk Hydro Grip setting spray.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:38.670
Mine is very well loved.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.230
This is overall a really
nice setting spray.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:42.830
It has more of a dewy finish to it,

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.960
so it melts makeup powders
really nicely into your skin,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.420
but it also does help
the makeup last longer.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.980
I like to spray this in layers

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.110
at different parts of
the application process

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.950
to really make sure nothing is
going to move around too much.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.830
The transfer is super minimal,
if you do get any at all,

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.450
and I just really like how my skin looks

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.090
when I use this setting spray.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.920
This is one of the coolest
products I've tried

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.040
in a really long time.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.160
This is the Genlen Beauty Facemud,

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.000
and it's this super matte, mousse-y cream

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.070
that can be applied to your
eyes, lips, and cheeks.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.730
It was kind of intimidating at first

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:16.870
because it's so pigmented
-- like, look at that --

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.740
but it was way easier to
control than I thought.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.030
You just go in little by little.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:22.230
You can go from like a wash of color,

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:23.770
like I did on my eyes and cheeks,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.210
to full-color payoff
like I did on my lips.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.680
It didn't remove any of the
product I already had on,

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.530
and I don't know, it's just
unique and easy to use.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.508
And I love the velvety finish it has.

